strings.syntax.while:
while commands; do commands; done   (until: as long as the commands do NOT succeed)
  n=0; while [ $n -lt 3 ]; do echo $n; n=$((n + 1)); done
  ls | while read -r name; do echo "- $name"; done

strings.syntax.function:
name() { commands; }   or   function name { commands; }
The arguments are $1, $2…, $@; "local" creates variables of the function, "return n" exits.
  greet() { echo "Hello, $1"; }; greet Eugenio

strings.syntax.variables:
name=value (no spaces), $name or ${name}. Arrays: a=(x y z), ${a[0]}, ${a[@]}, ${#a[@]}.
${v:-default} ${v:=default} ${v:+alt} ${#v} ${v#prefix} ${v%suffix} ${v/from/to} ${v//from/to} ${v:start:length} ${v^^} ${v,,}
Special: $? status of the last command, $$ the shell, $! the last command in the background, $# $@ $* the arguments.

strings.file.command.text:
«{name}» runs this command when it opens:

{command}

Run it only if you trust who made the link. Continue?

